# Bimedian theorem — the two bimedians of a quadrilateral (joining midpoints of opposite sides) bisect each other (source: classical; Altshiller-Court)
A B C = triangle
D = free
P = midpoint(A, B)
Q = midpoint(C, D)
R = midpoint(B, C)
S = midpoint(D, A)
X = meet(line(P, Q), line(R, S))
prove cong(X, P, X, Q)
